sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task; DECISIONS R1 + round 2 websocket.sync (no Swamp run, the Gateway closes the task from Reverb's own reports). docs/reference/websocket-apps.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: websocket:app:destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant N as Reverb<br/>on websocket Node
  CLI->>GW: websocket:app:destroy<br/>hauzer --force
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit websocket:app:destroy hauzer --force`
  %%> - syntax: `<name> [--force] [--operation-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--force`, the CLI asks first; the default is No
  %%> - without a terminal, or with `--json`, `--force` is required (`websocket.confirmation_required`)
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Delete app, revision 20<br/>R1: no run · task #5151
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the app is not `gateway` (`websocket.app_reserved`)
  %%> - no Instance uses the app (`websocket.app_in_use`); remove it with `instance:websocket:remove` first
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - deletes the app and its encrypted secret, and saves registry revision 20, in one transaction
  %%> - records task #5151, which waits for revision 20
  %%> Why no Swamp run:
  %%> - nothing has to be done on a Node; Reverb pulls the registry itself (R1)
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5151
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  loop each Reverb reconcile, 30 s
    N->>GW: Pull the registry<br/>full snapshot, revision 20
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - every Reverb process fetches the full snapshot on its own 30-second reconcile
    %%> - it stops accepting the app and closes only that app's sockets with code `4001`
    %%> - other apps keep their connections; Reverb does not restart
    N->>GW: Report applied revision<br/>per process and boot
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - each process reports the revision it applied, with its boot identity
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the app only counts as gone when no serving process accepts it anymore
  end
  alt every process applied 20
    Note over GW: Close the task<br/>succeeded · app revoked
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no serving Reverb process accepts the app
    %%> - task #5151 succeeds
  else no fresh report in 5 min
    Note over GW: Close the task, failed<br/>websocket.registry_pending
    %%> When:
    %%> - a serving process is stale or missing
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5151 fails; the app stays deleted in the Gateway
    %%> - a process that still runs an older snapshot may accept the app until it reconciles; status reports show the pending revocation
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run `websocket:sync` after the fix
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5151
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
